#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""abook - download audiobooks (yt-dlp directly, or vydra) and merge multi-part books into one
.m4a (AAC, default) / .mp3 with chapters; verify the library (SHA-256, decode, completeness).

Usage:
    abook get <manifest.json>...       [--only ID ...] [--dry-run] [--retry-failed]
                                        [--jobs N] [--bitrate {128,192,256,320}] [--state PATH]
                                        [--engine direct|vydra]   (default direct: yt-dlp → .m4a)
    abook verify [--quick|--full] [--fix] [--no-net] [--json] [<manifest.json>...]
    abook status [<manifest.json>...]  [--state PATH]
    abook notes <manifest.json>...     [--state PATH]
    abook sync                         [--db PATH] [--out-dir DIR]
    abook aidoc                        [--db PATH] [--out-dir DIR] [--lite]
    abook review                       [--port 8790] [--no-browser] [--db PATH] [--out-dir DIR]

`sync` imports ~/abook/manifests/*.json (+ F-buldakov-top.json) and state.json
(read-only) into ~/abook/library.db (SQLite, WAL, FTS5). `review` is a local web
app (127.0.0.1) for reviews/ratings/queue/stats; every change regenerates
Аудиокниги/БИБЛИОТЕКА_ДЛЯ_ИИ.md (+ _lite.md) — a dump of the DB for an AI assistant.

State, logs and staging live in ~/abook/ (staging on ext4, final files go to
/mnt/d/VideoDownloader/Аудиокниги/<section>/). Override the state file with
--state or $ABOOK_STATE (useful for testing without touching a live run; the log and
staging then live next to that state file). Point the library root elsewhere with
--library DIR or $ABOOK_LIBRARY (tests / a scratch "D:").

Integrity: parts are ordered explicitly (url_index, playlist_index) and checked (duplicates,
playlist gaps, numbered titles going backwards, truncation vs. the source's duration); the
merged file is checked (duration, chapters, full decode, silences, payload size); its SHA-256
is compared after copying to the library and recorded in state.json and CHECKSUMS.sha256.

stdlib only, no third-party dependencies.
"""
